<title>CHILE: Chile posts $23.4 mln January trade surplus.</title>
<headline>Chile posts $23.4 mln January trade surplus.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile posted a $23.4 million trade surplus in January compared with a $88.6-million deficit in the same month 1996, said the central bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>The figures showed exports rising to $1.47 billion from $1.27 billion in January 1996.</p>
<p>Imports rose to $1.45 billion from $1.36 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
